meta {
  name: Update Asset
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

patch {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/assets/6aa021b72b6fd055ffb7ca9f
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "alt_text": "WC test asset UPDATED",
    "filename": "wc_test_asset_renamed.jpg",
    "category_ids": ["6a9f1b862b6fd055ffb7c7de"]
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.data.alt_text: eq WC test asset UPDATED
  res.body.data.categories: isArray
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-08 against the kept asset fixture. `200 OK` --
  matches `openapi_pimv3.json`'s declared status, contradicts `API
  V3.md`'s stated 204-for-patch convention.

  `alt_text`/`filename` update as expected. **`category_ids` here DOES
  link** (`data.categories` comes back non-empty, and a follow-up `GET
  /assets/{id}/categories` confirms the full expanded category object) --
  unlike the identical field silently ignored on `POST` (see "Create
  Asset.bru"). The `categories` field on this PATCH response is a shallow
  reference (`[{"id": "..."}]`), while the `/categories` subpath returns
  the fully expanded object -- same shallow-vs-expanded split seen
  elsewhere in this API (e.g. products' `product_relationships` field vs.
  its `/relationships` subpath).

  **Update (2026-09-15)**: `PATCH` is now formally declared in
  `openapi_pimv3.json`'s refreshed spec (it was already declared before
  this refresh too, unlike most of this session's other resources -- see
  quirk list). This file previously had no `example{}` block; the
  `example` below was captured fresh against a disposable scratch asset
  (not the kept fixture, to avoid mutating it further) confirming the
  same `alt_text`/`filename` PATCH behavior described above.
}

example {
  name: Update Asset - Success (alt_text/filename)
  description: Real response captured 2026-09-15 against a disposable scratch asset on "David's Dev Account" (not the kept fixture).

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/assets/6aa98267a30ca5945169a24f
    method: patch
    mode: json
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Content-Type: application/json
      Accept: application/json
    }
    body:json: {
      {
        "alt_text": "WC test asset alt text",
        "filename": "wc_test_patch_delete_asset_renamed.jpg"
      }
    }
  }

